ry of colorectal polyps and masses: Rediscovered truths from the barium enema era</article-title><source>AJR Am J Roentgenol</source><year>2007</year><volume>188</volume><fpage>619</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17312044</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tony</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Harish</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramachandran</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sunilkumar</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Profile of colonic polyps in a southern indian population</article-title><source>Indian J Gastroenterol</source><year>2007</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>127</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17704579</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lieberman</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bond</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahnen</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Garewal</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Chejfec</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of colonoscopy to screen asymptomatic adults for colorectal cancer. Veterans affairs cooperative study group 380</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>343</volume><fpage>162</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10900274</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li